{"review_id": "233866831", "user_id": "e75be960b2902f1322e600124c171f1732c309e5b9eb0b5ca9f159f8b9f11aa2", "item_id": "238960", "item_title": "Path of Exile", "timestamp": 1787879152, "timestamp_updated": 1787879152, "timestamp_precision": "second", "event_time_lower_utc": 1787879152, "available_after_utc": 1787879152, "edit_time_status": "not_shown_assumed_unedited", "crawl_time_utc": "2026-11-21T11:41:48.033754Z", "source_feedback": true, "positive_interaction": true, "title": "", "text": "1", "language": "unknown", "helpful_votes": null, "source_url": "https://steamcommunity.com", "source_method": "public_profile_listing_with_api_seed_timestamps", "text_available_after_utc": 1787925600}
{"review_id": "229757831", "user_id": "e75be960b2902f1322e600124c171f1732c309e5b9eb0b5ca9f159f8b9f11aa2", "item_id": "230410", "item_title": "Warframe", "timestamp": 1783296000, "timestamp_updated": 1783296000, "timestamp_precision": "day", "event_time_lower_utc": 1783245600, "available_after_utc": 1783432800, "edit_time_status": "shown_on_public_page", "crawl_time_utc": "2026-11-21T11:41:49.728070Z", "source_feedback": false, "positive_interaction": false, "title": "", "text": "The game itself is great. I'm posting a negative review just to vent about the long, unskippable free-roam questlines. Holy sh!t, I've never seen such mediocre, nonsensical drivel in my life.\nStart with this: the moment you talk to any NPC, they launch into their entire life story, and you can't skip it. That would be fine if there were even a breadcrumb of something engaging, funny, or thought-provoking in there. There isn't. Nothing. Every time an NPC opens their mouth, I suddenly want to go wash dishes or take out the trash, because both are more entertaining than this low-effort yapping.\nThen there are the questlines themselves. For example, the very first one is a love triangle between three old geezers, delivered in the flattest, most uninspired way imaginable:\n1. Grandpa A asks you to find missing Grandpa B, who's married to Grandma C.\n2. Grandma C thinks Grandpa A killed Grandpa B and hates him for it.\n3. While searching for Grandpa B, you find a locket containing the item Grandpa A once used to propose to Grandpa B's wife (Grandma C).\n4. Grandma C is now in love with Grandpa A. Everyone's happy.\nHuh?\nOn top of that, all of it is buried under nonstop filler dialogue. This isn't the millennial style where a character cracks a \"witty\" line every other sentence -- here it's more like every tenth line, and the rest is just empty, useless filler you're forced to sit through unless you mute it in the settings (thank god that's an option). Imagine being tied to a chair while the most untalented, forgettable writer alive reads you his debut novel -- that's the experience. It would almost be better if the dialogue were so bad it was funny, at least that'd be entertaining. Instead it's just bad -- painfully, soul-crushingly mediocre.\nNone of this would matter if it were skippable, but it isn't. You'll sit for five minutes listening to a rightfully bored voice actor read boring lines, over and over. And then there's the back-and-forth between loading zones, because NPCs always need to tell you something in person -- even though they had no problem calling you thirty seconds earlier.\nWhy do so many good games have this one spoonful of pure idiocy sitting right in the middle of otherwise solid design?", "language": "unknown", "helpful_votes": null, "source_url": "https://steamcommunity.com", "source_method": "public_profile_review_listing"}
